{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>They set</b> — The lamed is light, even though it is from the heavy binyan, like 'they sought my soul' [Psalms 35:4] [בקשו נפשי]. Ibn Bil'am said: for this is inverted, the correct reading being 'they set fire in your sanctuary' [שלחו אש במקדשך]. It is also possible that the reason is that the fire was all around, and it is as if the sanctuary were sent [into the fire]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 74, :notes {0 "Resolved הלמ\"ד as referring to the lamed in שלחו; 'Ibn Bil'am' is preserved as the epithet without expansion, following the instruction to keep disputes and names as found."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:25.819774933Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}